# Line-ending normalization.
#
# The Docker build (docker/Dockerfile.juicelab) applies patches/juicelab-core.patch
# and the overlay/ tree to a juice-shop checkout INSIDE a Linux container with
# `git apply --3way`. Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which
# rewrites LF -> CRLF on checkout. A CRLF patch (or CRLF overlay source) does not
# apply to the LF juice-shop sources and `git apply` fails on every hunk:
#   error: patch failed: config/default.yml:458
#   error: <file>: patch does not apply
# Forcing LF on checkout for all text files makes the build deterministic on
# Windows / macOS / Linux alike.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Build-critical: must always be LF regardless of platform or local git config.
*.patch text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.scss  text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf

# Binaries — never normalize.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.svg   binary
*.docx  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.otf   binary
